# NVIDIA's MXFP8 recipe (Transformer Engine's MXFP8BlockScaling): every projection
# inside a block in E4M3, the gradients too, with a power-of-two scale per 32 values,
# rounded up. Softmax attention's own matmuls, the embedding, the head and the router
# stay in bfloat16; the routed experts multiply in MXFP8 too, by a grouped GEMM. A run
# uses it by name, next to an architecture:
#
#   use llama3_8b
#   use nvidia_mxfp8
precision = precision(compute=bfloat16, matmuls=mxfp8, roles=roles(experts=mxfp8))
